 ## Modeling Notes
 
 - **Account vs member:** `users` is the login account (Laravel Auth); `entity_memberships` is the user's link to the entity with role.
-- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
-- **Owner and circular FK:** `entities.owner_membership_id` points to the membership with `role = owner`. Since `entity_memberships.entity_id` references `entities`, the FK is circular — on bootstrap, create entity with `owner_membership_id` null, create owner membership, then fill the FK (or use deferrable constraint). Ownership transfer updates this FK and involved roles.
+- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced by the unique `(entity_id, user_id)` constraint; there is no global UK on `user_id`.
+- **One owner, enforced by the database:** `entity_memberships.owner_seq` is a stored generated column that evaluates to `1` when `role = 'owner'` and `NULL` otherwise. The unique index `entity_memberships_one_owner` on `(entity_id, owner_seq)` rejects a second owner for the same entity while allowing any number of non-owners (SQLite and MariaDB both ignore `NULL` in unique indexes). Different entities may each have their own owner. Ownership transfer updates the old owner's role and the new owner's role in the same transaction; deleting an owner membership is never allowed.
+- **Soft deletes:** `entities` uses soft deletes (`deleted_at`); memberships are only removed by cascade on hard delete of the entity or the user, or explicitly through the membership policy.
+- **Tenant authorization:** `App\Policies\EntityPolicy` and `App\Policies\EntityMembershipPolicy` translate memberships into permissions: any member may view, owner/admin may update/delete entities and assign roles, only the owner manages settings, and an owner membership can never be deleted. The owner may also remove themselves only after transferring ownership (their membership is still the owner membership until then).
 - **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
 - **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
 - **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
@@ -158,5 +162,5 @@ ## Modeling Notes
 - **Payments:** `payments` tracks each charge generated by subscription; status synced with Asaas (PENDING, RECEIVED, REFUNDED, CANCELED, OVERDUE).
 - **Billing account:** `cpf_cnpj` stores fiscal data for invoice generation.
 - **Enums:** `role` (`admin`, `owner`, `employee`); `subscriptions.status`; `tickets.channel`; `tickets.status` — values in business rules.
-- **Unique constraints:** `billing_accounts (entity_id)`; `entity_memberships (entity_id, user_id)`; `queues (entity_id, slug)`; `queue_access (entity_membership_id, queue_id)`; `tickets (queue_id, code)` per issuance window; `payments (asaas_payment_id)`; `subscriptions (billing_account_id)` (1:1).
+- **Unique constraints:** `entities (slug)` as `entities_slug_unique`; `entity_memberships (entity_id, user_id)` as `entity_memberships_entity_user_unique`; `entity_memberships (entity_id, owner_seq)` as `entity_memberships_one_owner`; `billing_accounts (entity_id)`; `queues (entity_id, slug)`; `queue_access (entity_membership_id, queue_id)`; `tickets (queue_id, code)` per issuance window; `payments (asaas_payment_id)`; `subscriptions (billing_account_id)` (1:1).
